hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20631","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there is no good in you, and a group of my ummah will remain aided, those who forsake them will not harm them, until the Hour comes."
"20632","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there is no good in you, and a group of my ummah will remain aided, those who forsake them will not harm them, until the Hour comes."
"20633","Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over my head."
"20634","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to us, from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I pity it, or he said: I pity the sheep to slaughter it. He said: And the sheep, if you show it mercy, Allah will show you mercy."
"20635","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting three days of every month is the fasting of the lifetime and its breaking."
"20636","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: A man used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of his. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you love him? He said: O Messenger of Allah, may Allah love you as I love him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and said: What has happened to the son of so-and-so? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he died. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his father: Would you not love that you not come to a gate of the gates of Paradise but find him waiting for you? The man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for all of us? He said: Rather for all of you."
"20637","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrate from his father that a man used to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"20638","Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Sham become corrupt there is no good in you, and people of my ummah will remain aided, they will not care who forsakes them, until the Hour comes."
"20639","Hasan meaning al-Ashyab and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, Abu al-Nadr said in his hadith: Zuhayr narrated to me, Urwah ibn Abd Allah ibn Qushayr Abu Mahal al-Ju'fi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Muzaynah and we pledged allegiance to him, and his shirt was unbuttoned. He said: So we pledged allegiance to him, then I put my hand into the opening of his shirt and touched the seal. Urwah said: I never saw Mu'awiyah nor his son, and I think he means Iyas, in winter at all nor in heat, except with their waist-wrappers unbuttoned, they would never button them."
"20640","Rawh narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrate from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked his permission to put my hand into his collar that he might supplicate for me. He did not prevent me, and I feeling him, that he supplicated for me. He said: I found upon the cartilage of his shoulder like a sil'ah growth."
"20641","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Iyas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he supplicated for him and wiped his head."
"20642","Wahb narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Concerning fasting three days of the month: the fast of the lifetime and its breaking."
